# =================================================================
# CONFIGURATION FOR QWEN3.8-27B DENSE, FULLY ON GPU - CUDA MODE
# =================================================================
# WHEN TO USE: best profile for PROGRAMMING, especially long autonomous runs.
#
#   + Much more reliable on long flows: follows the directives to the end,
#     rarely stalls, loops far less, and does not claim "done" early. Same
#     OpenCode task (stdlib inventory service, hidden 12-check acceptance
#     test): finished alone in 17 min, 12/12, verified its own work.
#     APEX-I-Mini on the identical task: stopped by hand at 27 min, 8/12.
#   - Speed: ~40 tok/s on a short context, ~33 tok/s at 96K, about half
#     the 35B A3B. Big file writes leave the screen idle for minutes; check
#     progress with: curl -s http://<host>:12345/slots | jq '.[0].next_token[0].n_decoded'
#   - No vision in this profile. The model supports it (unsloth ships an
#     mmproj, ~0.9 GB), but there is no VRAM left for it next to the weights.
#   - 96K context instead of 128K. At 100K (102400) generation fell to ~2 tok/s
#     on the reference host (11.9 GB of 12.28 GB VRAM used), so 96K is the limit.
#
# For interactive assistants, agents and image/video analysis, use
# qwen3.6-35b-a3b-apex-mini-best-assistant-with-vision instead.
#
# Dense 27B kept entirely in 12 GB of VRAM: UD-Q2_K_XL weights plus a single
# 96K slot. See the header of the compose file for the memory arithmetic.
# Launch with: ./scripts/docker/launch-server.sh .env.gpu.qwen3.8-27b-fullgpu-best-coding

COMPOSE_FILE=docker/docker-compose-gpu-qwen-27b-fullgpu.yml

HF_REPO="unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-GGUF"
HF_FILE="Qwen3.8-27B-UD-Q2_K_XL.gguf"

LLAMA_HOST=127.0.0.1
LLAMA_PORT=12345

# One 96K slot. OpenCode reads the real value from /slots at startup.
LLAMA_CONTEXT_SIZE=98304

LLAMA_CPU_THREADS=14

MODELS_DIR=""
